<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dornbirn</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dornbirn is the largest town in the Austrian state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vorarlberg">Vorarlberg</a>, lying in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> valley east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-constance">Lake Constance</a>. The lords of Ems held castles above it in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, and it came under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rule in the late 14th century. From the 19th century it grew into a centre of the textile industry, and it is now the economic hub of the region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dornbirn.jpg" alt="Dornbirn" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Feel free to use my photos, but please mention me as the author and if you want send me a message. or (rufre@lenz-nen... · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Watzenegg7.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
